#   MDP-memoryless        P1=0 P2=0 P3=1 P4=3 P5=3 P6=1 P7=4 P8=0 P9=0 P10=4 P11=0 P12=4  ← VIOLATES fairness
#   greedy-Hungarian      P1=1 P2=1 P3=2 P4=2 P5=2 P6=2 P7=2 P8=2 P9=2 P10=2 P11=0 P12=2
#   LP-relaxation         P1=2 P2=0 P3=2 P4=2 P5=2 P6=2 P7=2 P8=2 P9=2 P10=2 P11=0 P12=2
#   IP/MIP-feasible       P1=2 P2=0 P3=2 P4=2 P5=2 P6=2 P7=2 P8=2 P9=2 P10=2 P11=0 P12=2
#   MDP-VI-exact          P1=2 P2=0 P3=2 P4=2 P5=2 P6=2 P7=2 P8=2 P9=2 P10=2 P11=0 P12=2

# Architectural recap:
#   random               → L3: trivial baseline, ignores fairness
#   MDP-memoryless       → L2 with state=(t,) — Markov but NO history → cannot express fairness
#   greedy-Hungarian     → L3: per-period bipartite assignment with fairness pre-fill
#   LP-relaxation        → L3: simplex / interior-point on the LP relaxation, Hungarian-rounded
#   IP/MIP-feasible      → L3: exact 0/1 IP/MIP branch-and-cut DES; time-boxed, returns best feasible incumbent
#   MDP-VI-exact         → L2 with state=(t, prev-bench) — Markov + 1-period memory ⇒ fairness
#
#   Layer 1 (DES): simulateMatchDES runs 80 game-minutes per match,
#                  samples Poisson goal events from on-field affinity,
#                  triggers a substitution event at every period boundary.
#   Layer 2 (MDP): exact backward induction; |S| = 4 periods × C(12,5) = 3168,
#                  reward at each (s, a) is the Hungarian-optimal assignment.
#   POMDP feature: hidden fatigue belief is carried across periods for audit metrics.
#   Layer 3:       random / greedy-Hungarian / LP-relaxation / IP-MIP / MDP-VI.


